  "original_lyrics": "[intro]\n(Bass):\n(n.)\n\n[verse]\nIf my man was fighting,\nSome unholy war,\nI would be be-hind him.\nStraight, shook up,\n\n[bridge]\nWith strength,\nHe didn't know,\nIt's you I'm fighting for.\n\n[chorus]\nHe can't lose,\nWith me in tow,\nI refuse,\nTo let him go.\nAt his side,\nAnd drunk on pride,\nWe wait for the blo-ow.\n\n[verse]\nWe put it in writing,\n\n[bridge]\nJust us on kitchen floor.\nJustice done,\nReciting,\nMy stomach standing still,\nLike you're reading my will.\n\n[chorus]\nHe still stands,\n\n[intro]\nHis scars say,\nI'll battle till,\nThis bitter finale.\nJust me, my dignity,\nAnd this guitar case.\n\n[verse]\nIf, if my man is fighting,\nSome un-holy war,\nAnd I will stand beside you.\n\n[bridge]\n, I would have died too;\nI' of liked to.\n\n[chorus]\nIf my man,\nWas fight-ing,\nSome un-holy war.\nIf my man was fighting.",
